# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in every diff.
#
# This project is developed on Windows and published to npm; a checkout that
# silently converts CRLF to LF (or back) makes every whitespace-only change
# look like a 30-line rewrite of the whole file, which buries the real diff.
#
# `text=auto` lets git store LF internally and check out the native ending.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files where the exact bytes matter: they are served to a browser or copied
# verbatim by tooling. `text` here means "still text, still LF in the repo" --
# it does NOT opt out of newline translation. To truly leave a file's bytes
# alone you would use `-text`; nothing here needs that, these entries only pin
# the text attribute explicitly so a future wildcard cannot flip them binary.
*.svg  text
*.json text
*.yml  text
*.md   text

# Binary-ish artefacts that must never be normalised.
*.tgz  binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
